        "id": "p10-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Write $\\dfrac{2x+3}{x-1}$ in the form $a+\\dfrac{b}{x-1}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$2+\\dfrac{5}{x-1}$",
          "worked": "The leading terms give the quotient $2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(2x+3)-2(x-1)&=2x+3-2x+2\\\\(2x+3)-2(x-1)&=5\\\\2x+3&=2(x-1)+5\\\\\\frac{2x+3}{x-1}&=2+\\frac{5}{x-1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Write $\\dfrac{4x^2+3x+2}{x^2+2x}$ in the form $a+\\dfrac{bx+c}{x^2+2x}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$4+\\dfrac{2-5x}{x^2+2x}$",
          "worked": "The leading terms give the quotient $4$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(4x^2+3x+2)-4(x^2+2x)&=4x^2+3x+2-4x^2-8x\\\\(4x^2+3x+2)-4(x^2+2x)&=-5x+2\\\\4x^2+3x+2&=4(x^2+2x)-5x+2\\\\\\frac{4x^2+3x+2}{x^2+2x}&=4+\\frac{-5x+2}{x^2+2x}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
